<title>INDIA: India soybean steady as markets shut for festival.</title>
<headline>India soybean steady as markets shut for festival.</headline>
<dateline>INDORE, India 1997-02-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Soybean prices were steady in central Indian markets on Wednesday, with many markets closed for a Hindu spring festival. Soybean prices were down 50-100 rupees per tonne in plant delivery condition.</p>
<p>Business volumes were dull. Soyoil prices rose 300 rupees per tonne on very limited supply from plants and refineries. The undertone was strong.</p>
<p>Soymeal prices were firm on limited supply. Soymeal yellow was quoted at $282-283 per tonne in export. Rapeseed extraction was $110 per tonne for ready shipment and was $105 for March-April shipment in export.</p>
<p>Rapeseed extraction was 3,700 rupees for ready delivery and was 3,600 rupees for March-April delivery in FOR (Free on Rail) condition.</p>
